### 1. **CharStreams.java** - Duplicate Copy Methods with Minor Variations
**File:** `/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/G003_guava/guava/src/com/google/common/io/CharStreams.java`

**Lines 110-121 (copyReaderToBuilder) and 138-149 (copyReaderToWriter):**

These two private static methods share nearly identical structure with only the target type difference:

```java
// Lines 110-121
static long copyReaderToBuilder(Reader from, StringBuilder to) throws IOException {
  checkNotNull(from);
  checkNotNull(to);
  char[] buf = new char[DEFAULT_BUF_SIZE];
  int nRead;
  long total = 0;
  while ((nRead = from.read(buf)) != -1) {
    to.append(buf, 0, nRead);      // target method call
    total += nRead;
  }
  return total;
}

// Lines 138-149
static long copyReaderToWriter(Reader from, Writer to) throws IOException {
  checkNotNull(from);
  checkNotNull(to);
  char[] buf = new char[DEFAULT_BUF_SIZE];
  int nRead;
  long total = 0;
  while ((nRead = from.read(buf)) != -1) {
    to.write(buf, 0, nRead);       // target method call
    total += nRead;
  }
  return total;
}
```

**Issue:** 100% duplication except for target method call (append vs write).

**Refactoring Suggestion:** Extract a private helper interface/functional approach:
```java
interface CharConsumer {
  void accept(char[] buf, int off, int len) throws IOException;
}

private static long copyReaderToTarget(Reader from, CharConsumer target) throws IOException {
  checkNotNull(from);
  checkNotNull(target);
  char[] buf = new char[DEFAULT_BUF_SIZE];
  int nRead;
  long total = 0;
  while ((nRead = from.read(buf)) != -1) {
    target.accept(buf, 0, nRead);
    total += nRead;
  }
  return total;
}

// Then:
static long copyReaderToBuilder(Reader from, StringBuilder to) throws IOException {
  return copyReaderToTarget(from, (buf, off, len) -> to.append(buf, off, len));
}

static long copyReaderToWriter(Reader from, Writer to) throws IOException {
  return copyReaderToTarget(from, (buf, off, len) -> to.write(buf, off, len));
}
```

