**Specific duplicated switch branches** (lines 334-365 in IntMath, 402-430 in LongMath):
- UNNECESSARY case handling and fallthrough
- DOWN case logic
- UP case logic
- CEILING/FLOOR cases with signum comparison
- HALF_EVEN/HALF_DOWN/HALF_UP cases with identical rounding logic

**Refactoring Suggestion:** Create a private shared rounding decision utility:
```java
// Shared utility in common package or create DivisionRoundingHelper
private static boolean shouldIncrement(
    long absRem,
    long absQ,
    RoundingMode mode,
    long div,
    int signum) {
  switch (mode) {
    case UNNECESSARY:
      checkRoundingUnnecessary(absRem == 0);
      // fall through
    case DOWN:
      return false;
    case UP:
      return true;
    case CEILING:
      return signum > 0;
    case FLOOR:
      return signum < 0;
    case HALF_EVEN:
    case HALF_DOWN:
    case HALF_UP:
      long cmpRemToHalfDivisor = absRem - (absQ - absRem);
      if (cmpRemToHalfDivisor == 0) {
        return mode == HALF_UP || (mode == HALF_EVEN & (div & 1) != 0);
      }
      return cmpRemToHalfDivisor > 0;
    default:
      throw new AssertionError();
  }
}
```

Then both divide methods call this shared utility instead of replicating the logic.

