  checkNotNull(c);
  checkNotNull(d);
  return concat(consumingForArray(a, b, c, d));
}
```

**Issue:** All three methods have identical logic: checkNotNull each iterator, then delegate to consumingForArray(). The only variation is the number of parameters.

**Refactoring Suggestion:** Extract a single private helper:
```java
private static <T extends @Nullable Object> Iterator<T> concatChecked(
    Iterator<? extends T>... iterators) {
  for (Iterator<? extends T> iterator : iterators) {
    checkNotNull(iterator);
  }
  return concat(consumingForArray(iterators));
}

// Then:
public static <T extends @Nullable Object> Iterator<T> concat(
    Iterator<? extends T> a, Iterator<? extends T> b) {
  return concatChecked(a, b);
}

public static <T extends @Nullable Object> Iterator<T> concat(
    Iterator<? extends T> a, Iterator<? extends T> b, Iterator<? extends T> c) {
  return concatChecked(a, b, c);
}

// etc.
```

---

## Summary Table

| File | Lines | Issue Type | Refactoring Approach |
|------|-------|-----------|----------------------|
| CharStreams.java | 110-149 | Identical copy methods | Extract shared helper with functional interface |
| Sets.java | 1198-1287 | Repeated filter patterns | Extract private generic filterImpl() helper |
| IntMath.java / LongMath.java | 313-367 / 384-435 | Duplicated divide() logic | Create shared rounding decision utility |
| MoreObjects.java | 210-262 | Repeated primitive wrappers | Extract addPrimitive() helper or parameterized version |
| Iterators.java | 504-546 | Repeated concat() boilerplate | Extract concatChecked() private helper |

All findings focus on **internal (private/package-private) code** where the refactoring would improve maintainability without affecting public API surface.

